# Input
```json
{
	"name": "my-package",
	"cpu": "x64",
	"cpu": ["x86_64"]
}

```

# Diagnostics
```
package.json:3:9 lint/nursery/usePackageJsonValidCpu ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The value of the cpu field isn't an array.
  
    1 │ {
    2 │ 	"name": "my-package",
  > 3 │ 	"cpu": "x64",
      │ 	       ^^^^^
    4 │ 	"cpu": ["x86_64"]
    5 │ }
  
  i Package managers expect a list of the processor types that the package supports. They compare the list with the processor type of the machine to decide whether the package can be installed there.
  
  i List the supported processor types in an array, for example ["x64", "arm64"].
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

```
package.json:4:10 lint/nursery/usePackageJsonValidCpu ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This entry of the cpu field isn't a known processor type.
  
    2 │ 	"name": "my-package",
    3 │ 	"cpu": "x64",
  > 4 │ 	"cpu": ["x86_64"]
      │ 	        ^^^^^^^^
    5 │ }
    6 │ 
  
  i Package managers compare each entry with the processor type of the machine to decide whether the package can be installed there. An entry that isn't a processor type never matches, so the package may be installed on, or refused by, the wrong machines.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Replace the entry with one of the following processor types, in quotes. To exclude a processor type instead, add ! before its name.
  
  - arm
  - arm64
  - ia32
  - loong64
  - mips
  - mipsel
  - ppc64
  - riscv64
  - s390
  - s390x
  - x64
  

```
